I wanted to make sure that the stability/trim can only be done under that specific saved file because, there needs to be a

general idea of what the plan of this aircraft needs to go to calculate the stability/trim. For example, based on my T/W 

constraint, I chose for my stability/trim:

  Wing area: 8.2000 (I chose this point above all the T/W constraints)

  Horizontal tail volume coefficient: 0.6300

  Vertical tail volume coefficient: 0.0360

  Cockpit radius: 0.6300

  Fuselage radius near tail: 0.3000

  Aspect Ratio Horizontal Stabilizer: 4

  Aspect Ratio Vertical Stabilizer: 1.8000

  Taper Ratio: 0.5000

  tail efficiency: 0.9000
  
  The tail efficiency tells the program of how well the horizontal stabilizer produce those forces when being compared to the 
  
  reference of the air flow. Highera the number between 0 to 1, the better the stability because of how well the horizontal 
  
  tail helps the pitching moment and the neutral point.

The results from this gave me:

  Tail moment arm: 2.2716
  
  Horizontal stabilizer wing area: 2.1488
  
  Horizontal stabilizer span: 2.9318
  
  Vertical stabilizer wing area: 1.1696
  
  Vertical stabilizer span: 1.451
  
  reference wing root chord: 1.2148
  
  reference wing tip chord: 0.60741
  
  Neutral location located at: 3.2118

The idea is that the user's inputs are a given set of requirements that are needed of the aircraft and then add in what the 

customer requests. 
